### Reviewer Notes & Suggestions

While the note is ready for submission, here are a few minor nitpicks you could consider addressing before uploading:

1. **[Minor] Terminology in Section 2.2:** You write that a chamber is bicolored "when it contains support vectors of both copies." In convex geometry, "support vectors" usually refers to the points on the boundary of the polytope that achieve the maximum (or the support hyperplanes themselves). Since the chamber consists of the dual normal directions, consider rephrasing to something like "when it contains normal directions maximizing each copy" or "linear objective vectors favoring each copy" to prevent any momentary cognitive dissonance for the reader.
2. **[Minor] Computational Engine Detail:** In Section 2.4, you mention "exact kernel computations in the quotient ring" and verification "modulo the Grassmann-Plücker ideal." A mathematically curious reader might appreciate a half-sentence or a parenthetical specifying the computational algebraic method used for this ideal membership test (e.g., standard Gröbner bases over $\mathbb{Q}$) since it is the engine of the 57,637 non-trivial certificates. 
